From: efx <volvox@stalya.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-efx: poll busy with CMD13

The Efinix controller's present state register does not follow DAT0, so
sdhci_card_busy() reports a card that is always busy. SD cards hardly ever
wait on it, but an eMMC does after every CMD6, and it never got past the
first one ("Card stuck being busy"). Drop card_busy so the core polls the
card's status with CMD13 instead.

---
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-efx.c	2026-09-23 15:21:00.622786592 +0300
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-efx.c	2026-09-23 15:21:00.628661094 +0300
@@ -286,6 +286,12 @@
 	device_property_read_u32(dev, "max-frequency", &pltfm_host->clock);
 
 	host->mmc_host_ops.get_cd = efx_sdhci_get_cd;
+	/*
+	 * The controller's present state does not follow DAT0, so sdhci's
+	 * card_busy() reads "busy" for good and an eMMC never gets past its
+	 * first CMD6. Without card_busy the core polls busy with CMD13.
+	 */
+	host->mmc_host_ops.card_busy = NULL;
 
 	ret = mmc_of_parse(host->mmc);
 	if (ret)
